{"type":"event","env":{"seq":15,"session":"20261118-120000-edges","created":1795003214200,"event":"item_completed","id":"m1","item":{"type":"message","text":"`Backoff::delay` took no `Rng`, so the jitter was whatever `thread_rng()` gave it.\n\n## What changed\n\n- The delay takes an `Rng`, so a test can seed it.\n\n- `cargo test -q upload` passes eleven of eleven, every run.\n\n- The jitter is half the base at most.\n\n```rust\npub fn delay(&self, attempt: u32, rng: &mut impl Rng) -> Duration {\n    let base = self.base * 2u32.pow(attempt);\n    base + Duration::from_millis(rng.gen_range(0..=base.as_millis() as u64 / 2))\n}\n```\n\n| Attempt | Before | After |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | 0 to 200 ms | 100 to 150 ms |\n| 3 | 0 to 800 ms | 400 to 600 ms |"}}}
